T:What it is
T:An island or
T:isle is a
T:piece of
T:land,
T:distinct
T:from a
T:continent,
T:completely
T:surrounded
T:by water.
T:There are
T:continental
T:islands,
T:which were
T:formed by
T:being split
T:from a
T:continent by
T:plate
T:tectonics,
T:and oceanic
T:islands,
T:which have
T:never been
T:part of a
T:continent.
T:Oceanic
T:islands can
T:be formed
T:from
T:volcanic
T:activity,
T:grow into
T:atolls from
T:coral reefs,
T:and form
T:from
T:sediment
T:along
T:shorelines,
T:creating
T:barrier
T:islands.
T:River
T:islands can
T:also form
T:from
T:sediment and
T:debris in
T:rivers.
T:Artificial
T:islands are
T:those made
T:by humans,
T:including
T:small rocky
T:outcroppings
T:built out of
T:lagoons and
T:large-scale
T:land
T:reclamation
T:projects
T:used for
T:development.
